# VectorNNTP core instructions

## Before changing anything

1. Identify the **actual target project** (today: primarily `VectorNNTP.NNTPD`). Do not assume every component shares architecture or invariants.
2. Inspect existing implementation, callers, consumers, ownership, lifecycle, and tests before editing.
3. Prefer the **smallest correct change**. Avoid speculative abstractions and unnecessary dependencies.
4. Preserve unrelated user changes and out-of-scope files.

## Project facts (inspect rather than invent)

- Solution: `VectorNNTP.NNTPD.sln`
- TFM: `net10.0`; nullable + implicit usings; `TreatWarningsAsErrors`; docs XML enabled (`Directory.Build.props`)
- Host: .NET Generic Host; options + `ValidateOnStart`; Serilog-exclusive logging
- Lifecycle: `ApplicationLifecycle` + `ApplicationServiceManager` + `IApplicationService` (see `docs/architecture.md`)
- Config contract: `docs/configuration.md` (authoritative over memory)
- Protocol data plane: **bytes throughout** — see `docs/architecture.md` § Byte-Oriented Protocol Data Plane
- NNTP standards library: `docs/standards/rfcs/` — read applicable RFC text before protocol work
- Experimental/historical material: `.artifacts/` (index: `.artifacts/ARTIFACT-INDEX.md`; policy: `.artifacts/REPOSITORY-ARTIFACT-POLICY.md`). Does not override `src/` / `tests/` / accepted `docs/`.

## BackFiller code style

All C# namespaces must be block-scoped; file-scoped namespaces are not permitted.

This applies to `src/VectorNNTP.BackFiller` and `tests/VectorNNTP.BackFiller.Tests`. Both projects set `csharp_style_namespace_declarations = block_scoped`.

## Common code style

All C# namespaces in `src/VectorNNTP.Common` and `tests/VectorNNTP.Common.Tests` must be block-scoped; file-scoped namespaces are not permitted. Both projects set `csharp_style_namespace_declarations = block_scoped`.

The namespace must match the folder under the project directory. `src/VectorNNTP.Common/Messaging/RabbitMq/Foo.cs` is `VectorNNTP.Common.Messaging.RabbitMq`. `tests/VectorNNTP.Common.Tests/Configuration/Foo.cs` is `VectorNNTP.Common.Tests.Configuration`. A file directly under the project directory uses that project's root namespace. `GlobalUsings.cs` has no namespace.

## Evidence and honesty

- Never claim builds, tests, format checks, benchmarks, or runtime verification succeeded unless they ran and succeeded here.
- Report limitations and unverified assumptions explicitly.
- Do not invent project conventions; inspect the repository.

## Byte-oriented protocol data plane

**Protocol data remains byte-oriented throughout the data plane.** Full rule: [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md#byte-oriented-protocol-data-plane).

- Incoming bytes are not converted to strings unless an explicit application/API/logging boundary requires it.
- Static outgoing protocol text is pre-encoded once and reused.
- Dynamic outgoing protocol fields remain bytes where possible.
- Do not construct a string merely to encode it back to bytes.
- Any bytes↔string conversion in a hot path requires an explicit justification. “The API currently takes a string” is not automatically sufficient — decide whether that API is an unnecessary protocol-layer boundary.

Strings are permitted at justified boundaries. They are not the default representation of protocol data.

## Source-generated structured logging

Prefer `LoggerMessageAttribute` + partial methods. Preserve structured properties; do not preformat log messages. Full rule: [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md#source-generated-structured-logging).

